    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0451" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg377"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Clay</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 2, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 2d ultimo, No. 73,
                    informing this department of the confirmation, by the Emperor, of the convention
                    between Messrs. Sibley and Collins and the Russian government, and of the orders
                    subsequently given for the admission of the men and material of the company into
                    the Russian possessions, has been received.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius M. Clay,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
